<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/lahaina-harbor.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/lahaina-harbor-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/lahaina-harbor.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.1"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/island-communities/">Island communities</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Lahaina &amp; West Maui</span></nav><p class="tag">Maui · West Maui</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser for Lahaina and West Maui Rebuilding</h1><p class="lede">West Maui families and associations are still working through the long process of rebuilding after August 2023. We help owners resolve disputes over the amount of their losses, with patience and respect.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn sun" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn line-light" href="/contact-hawaii-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Maui County</dd></div><div><dt>Island</dt><dd>Maui</dd></div><div><dt>Service</dt><dd>On-site inspections</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose"><div class="local"><div><b class="h">Local claim risks</b><ul class="chips"><li>Wildfire and total loss</li><li>Smoke and ash damage</li><li>Downslope wind events</li><li>Condo and resort water losses</li></ul></div><div><b class="h">Neighborhoods we cover</b><ul class="chips soft"><li>Lahaina town</li><li>Launiupoko</li><li>Kaanapali</li><li>Honokowai</li><li>Kahana</li><li>Napili</li><li>Kapalua</li></ul></div><p><b>Housing:</b> West Maui includes historic Lahaina homes and buildings, plantation-era and multigenerational family homes, resort condominiums along Kaanapali and Napili, and newer subdivisions on the slopes.</p><p><b>History:</b> On August 8, 2023, wind-driven fires destroyed much of Lahaina as strong downslope winds blew across Maui while Hurricane Dora passed far to the south.</p></div>
<h2>Rebuilding West Maui</h2>
<p>The August 2023 wildfire changed Lahaina profoundly. The fire, driven by strong downslope winds as Hurricane Dora passed far to the south, destroyed much of the historic town and the neighborhoods around it. For many families, the loss included homes that had been in the family for generations, often expanded over the years with ohana units and additions for relatives.</p>
<p>West Maui also includes Kaanapali, Honokowai, Kahana, Napili and Kapalua to the north, where resort condominiums and homes were largely spared by the flames but some experienced smoke, ash and soot. Launiupoko and the slopes above town include single-family homes and agricultural lots. Each of these settings brings different claim issues, from total-loss rebuilds to cleaning and contents disputes.</p>
<h2>Where rebuild claims get stuck</h2>
<p>Rebuilding after a disaster of this scale takes years, and insurance claims often run alongside permitting, debris removal and a stretched contractor market. Many owners find that the gap between their policy limits, the insurer’s valuation and the real cost to rebuild in West Maui today is wider than expected.</p>
<ul>
<li>Dwelling valuations that rely on generic cost data rather than current West Maui rebuild costs.</li>
<li>Ordinance-or-law and code-upgrade costs required for permits but left out of estimates.</li>
<li>Contents inventories reduced by heavy depreciation or disputed item values.</li>
<li>Additional living expense timelines that do not match the actual pace of rebuilding.</li>
<li>Smoke and ash claims in Kaanapali and Napili condos where cleaning scopes are disputed.</li>
<li>Replacement cost holdbacks and deadlines to complete repairs.</li>
</ul>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Deadlines and legal questions</b>Many policies contain deadlines for completing repairs, recovering held-back replacement cost or filing suit, and some may have been extended. If you are near any deadline, or your claim has been denied in whole or part, talk with a Hawaii attorney. We are not a law firm.</div>
<h2>How appraisal may help</h2>
<p>When an insurer accepts that a loss is covered but disagrees on how much it is worth, the appraisal clause can provide a structured way to resolve the amount. Appraisal does not decide coverage, policy limits or claim-handling questions, and it offers no guaranteed outcome. It can, however, put a detailed, locally priced estimate in front of a neutral process.</p>
<p>Hawaii Insurance Appraiser approaches West Maui claims with care for what owners have been through. We document pre-loss construction from photos, permits and family records, price rebuilding at current Maui costs including freight and General Excise Tax, and work on contents and smoke claims as well. Our <a href="/appraisal-specialties/wildfire-claim-appraisal/">wildfire claim appraisal</a> service explains the process, the <a href="/island-claim-tools/rcv-acv-holdback-calculator/">RCV, ACV and holdback calculator</a> helps you understand withheld amounts, and our guide on <a href="/hawaii-claim-guides/documenting-wildfire-smoke-damage/">documenting wildfire smoke damage</a> is useful for condo owners.</p>
<p>There is no single timeline for recovery, and every family’s situation is different. If you are not ready to think about appraisal yet, that is understandable. When you are, we can review your policy, the insurer’s figures and your records and explain your options in plain language.</p>
<h2>Specialties available in Lahaina &amp; West Maui</h2><p>Every Hawaii Insurance Appraiser specialty is available to owners and associations in Lahaina &amp; West Maui, including:</p><ul class="cols2"><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/appraisal-clause-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/homeowner-claim-appraisal/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/condo-aoao-commercial-appraisal/">Condo, AOAO &amp; Commercial</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/roof-hail-claim-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Claims</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/kona-storm-high-wind-claims/">Kona Storm &amp; High-Wind Claims</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/hurricane-claim-appraisal/">Hurricane Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/water-damage-claim-appraisal/">Water Damage Claims</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/fire-smoke-claim-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Claims</a></li></ul>
<h2>Questions from Lahaina &amp; West Maui owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Can appraisal help if my Lahaina home was a total loss?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>Appraisal may help if the insurer accepts coverage but disputes the cost to rebuild or the value of contents. Questions about policy limits or coverage are separate and are best discussed with a Hawaii attorney.</p></div></details><details><summary>My Kaanapali condo had smoke and ash but no fire damage. Is appraisal an option?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>If the insurer accepts the smoke claim but disagrees on the cleaning or replacement scope, appraisal may resolve the amount. Good documentation of soot and affected items helps.</p></div></details><details><summary>How do code upgrades affect rebuilding costs in West Maui?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>Current building codes and permit requirements can add cost beyond a like-for-like rebuild. Ordinance-or-law coverage, if your policy includes it, may pay for some of that additional cost up to its limit.</p></div></details></div>
